# [Component name] Spec

## Overview
One sentence: rendered tag + purpose.

Example: "A button-like action primitive rendered as `<button>`, dispatching an `onClick` handler when clicked."

## API

### Props
- `propA` (type): Purpose + constraints. Defaults to X.
- `propB` (type): Purpose + constraints. Only meaningful when `propA='...'`.
- `children` (ReactNode): Content projected into the component.

### Slots / Projection (if applicable)
Describe named slots, compound components, or content projection patterns.

## Behavior

### Default state
- Visual appearance when no props are set
- State of interactive elements (buttons, inputs, etc.)
- Responsive behavior across viewport sizes

### [Interaction / Behavior 1]
Step-by-step flow. Include timing if relevant (e.g., "animation takes 300ms").

### [Edge case: Null / Empty / Large content]
How does it behave with edge inputs?

### Responsive
- Below 600px: stacked layout, single column, etc.
- Above 600px: multi-column, side-by-side, etc.
- Animation / motion: freeze or adapt below 600px? (check `prefers-reduced-motion`)

## Accessibility

### Semantic HTML
- Rendered tag(s): e.g., `<button>`, `<fieldset>`, `<nav>`
- Implicit roles: e.g., Button renders `<button role="button">` (implicit, no redundant ARIA)

### ARIA (if needed)
- `aria-label`: When present? What does it announce?
- `aria-describedby`: Links to description or hint text
- `aria-expanded`: Collapsible content?
- `aria-invalid` / `aria-required`: Form fields?
- Live regions (`aria-live`, `aria-atomic`): Notifications, status updates?

### Keyboard
- Is it focusable? Tab order?
- Does it respond to arrow keys, Enter, Esc?
- Focus management: focus trap? Focus return?

### Screen Reader
- What does SR announce for default state?
- What does SR announce on interaction?
- Is name/role/value clear?

### Visual
- Color contrast: text, icons, borders (WCAG AA minimum 4.5:1)
- Motion: animations respect `prefers-reduced-motion`
- Touch targets: minimum 48×48 CSS px (touch-friendly)

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] Renders correct HTML structure per spec
- [ ] Accepts and validates all documented props
- [ ] Handles edge cases (null, undefined, empty content, very long text)
- [ ] Responsive behavior works below 600px and above
- [ ] All interactions work (click, keyboard, focus)
- [ ] Accessibility: semantic HTML, ARIA only if needed, keyboard accessible, SR announces correctly
- [ ] WCAG 2.0 AA: contrast, motion, zoom, form labels
- [ ] Tests pass (unit, a11y audit)

## Testing Strategy

### Unit tests
- Props validation (required, type constraints)
- Edge cases (null, undefined, empty, overflow)
- Computed state (e.g., disabled when X)
- Callbacks fire correctly (onChange, onClick, etc.)

### Integration tests
- Renders without crashing
- Compound component composition (if applicable)

### Visual regression tests
- Default state
- Prop variants (size, tone, state)
- Responsive (600px breakpoint)
- Dark mode (if applicable)

### Accessibility tests
- axe audit (automated)
- Keyboard navigation (manual or keyboard testing library)
- Screen reader announcements (manual or SR testing library)
